No — validation happens locally before any upload. The docs state inputs are "validated against the schema before anything is uploaded: required present, number in range..." (docs/features/job-inputs.md:26-29). In code, `small run` calls `inputs.validate(cfg.inputs, flags)` (packages/cli/bin/small.js:319) which checks `min`/`max` for `number` types and throws `--threshold 2 out of range (0–1)` immediately (packages/cli/lib/inputs.js:55-61) — this happens before the file-size cap check or the `POST /api/runs` call is ever made (packages/cli/bin/small.js:327-339). So with threshold=2 against a schema max of 1, the CLI will reject the run and exit with an error before your photo is read or uploaded; there's no "let the job reject it" path — the job process never starts.

Next step: fix the `--threshold` flag to be ≤1 (or edit the schema's `max` if 2 is actually a valid value for this job) and rerun.

