No — the CLI validates inputs before any upload happens. `--threshold 2` against a schema with `max = 1` fails the number-range check in `inputs.validate` and throws before the request is built or files are read (packages/cli/lib/inputs.js:58-60; packages/cli/bin/small.js:319, which calls `validate` prior to constructing the FormData/body at line 330+). This matches the original spec's requirement that range errors surface "before anything is uploaded" (m5646) and was confirmed shipped in the "CLI half" report, which specifically calls out range-error rejection happening pre-upload (m5831).

So don't bother uploading the photo — fix the flag to `--threshold 1` (or whatever value is ≤1) and rerun `small run`. Note: this range check is CLI-side only in this snapshot; the control-plane/runtime halves (job runner, R2 storage, outputs routes) were explicitly deferred and marked pending (m5670, m5887, docs/features/job-inputs.md:62-71), so there's no server-side re-validation to fall back on yet if the CLI check were bypassed.

