{"answer":"No. In this snapshot only six input types are supported: `file`, `number`, `select`, `date`, `text`, `bool` (docs/features/job-inputs.md:21; packages/cli/lib/inputs.js:6). `checkSchema` explicitly rejects anything else with a one-line error ("unknown type ... — one of file, number, select, date, text, bool") at both `small init` and `small deploy` time (packages/cli/lib/inputs.js:8-13; packages/cli/bin/small.js:187). Neither `csv` nor `multiselect` exist as types, so declaring one in `small.toml` would fail schema validation before the deploy proceeds.

Recorded intent notes multiselect was deliberately deferred: "Multiple selects — ponytail: single select covers the known apps; add `multiple = true` when one needs it" (docs/features/job-inputs.md:86). There's no mention of a csv type being considered or deferred — it's simply outside the closed set of six.

Next step: if you need multi-value selection, that's a documented future extension (`multiple = true` on `select`), not something you can add today. For CSV-like structured input, you'd currently have to use `type = "file"` and parse it in the job script, or use `text` with a pattern if it's a short list."],"citations":[{"kind":"code","path":"docs/features/job-inputs.md","start_line":21,"end_line":22},{"kind":"code","path":"packages/cli/lib/inputs.js","start_line":6,"end_line":13},{"kind":"code","path":"docs/features/job-inputs.md","start_line":86,"end_line":86}]}
